1
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:07,403
You know how much your site spent today.

2
00:00:07,853 --> 00:00:12,631
But was the work done for that money? That is the real question.

3
00:00:13,081 --> 00:00:19,652
Say four masons and two helpers. One day's wages: ₹6,400.

4
00:00:20,102 --> 00:00:27,441
Was ₹6,400 worth of work done? Until now, nobody had a clear answer.

5
00:00:27,891 --> 00:00:34,376
Mesiri Cost control answers it, for every BOQ item, every day.

6
00:00:34,826 --> 00:00:40,202
In the dashboard, Cost control sits below Finance, with six pages.

7
00:00:40,652 --> 00:00:51,745
Site engineers type nothing new: the work, attendance, materials and bills they already send on WhatsApp are the data.

8
00:00:52,195 --> 00:00:57,059
The Overview lists every project, worst first.

9
00:00:57,509 --> 00:01:08,091
Green Villa says Watch: at today's rate it will finish about ₹3.9 lakh over budget.

10
00:01:08,541 --> 00:01:11,954
Lake View Apartments is on budget.

11
00:01:12,404 --> 00:01:22,644
It starts from the BOQ: each item's quantity, client rate and budget rate, the work done, and the budget it earned.

12
00:01:23,094 --> 00:01:36,577
When today's work comes in, Mesiri suggests its BOQ line. One click confirms it. Nothing is counted on a guess, or twice.

13
00:01:37,027 --> 00:01:47,267
Green / red is the GM's page. Each day is green or red: the labour spent against the labour budget the work earned.

14
00:01:47,717 --> 00:02:05,722
Then every BOQ line, worst first, with the reason. Electrical conduits: ₹11,950 of labour for 44 points. ₹272 a point, against a budget of ₹96. Red.

15
00:02:06,172 --> 00:02:11,292
Plinth beam is green: the work was worth more than the labour it took.

16
00:02:11,742 --> 00:02:17,715
Labour nobody has put on a BOQ line is shown apart. It is never guessed into a line.

17
00:02:18,165 --> 00:02:28,747
Putting it on a line takes a moment: pick the line and the man-days, press Put on line. A day can be split over several lines.

18
00:02:29,197 --> 00:02:38,839
Budget vs actual gives the full picture: budget, earned, spent, and the forecast at completion.

19
00:02:39,289 --> 00:02:50,383
Here labour is under budget, but materials are ₹66,000 over what the work has earned. That needs a look now.

20
00:02:50,833 --> 00:03:03,206
Materials vs BOQ checks each material against what the work needed by the BOQ norms. Cement: the work needed 364 bags; 418 were used.

21
00:03:03,656 --> 00:03:13,640
It also says what is still needed to finish, beyond stock and open orders, so a shortage shows up early.

22
00:03:14,090 --> 00:03:27,743
Cost centres shows where the money went: materials, labour, machines, fuel, site overheads. Its total matches Finance exactly.

23
00:03:28,193 --> 00:03:36,641
If a category has no cost centre, Mesiri says so openly. The owner fixes it in one click.

24
00:03:37,091 --> 00:03:45,027
Budget vs actual and Green / red export to Excel, for the CA and the MD.

25
00:03:45,477 --> 00:03:56,656
Every evening the owner and project manager get a cost card on WhatsApp, and can ask Mesiri how cost is going today.

26
00:03:57,106 --> 00:04:10,589
Money is for the owner, admin, finance and project managers. A site engineer sees their own site's green or red and quantities, never the money.

27
00:04:11,039 --> 00:04:16,756
Know where costs are running over, before you release the payment.

28
00:04:17,206 --> 00:04:22,838
Mesiri Cost control: make sure every rupee spent gets its work done.

